          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On October 26, 2004, around 2:15 PM, a driver on the highway suddenly felt observed and, when he turned his head, he was intrigued by the presence of gray circular shapes in a cloud. These shapes moved like fan blades and made him think of \"an eye.\" The observation was intermittent over several seconds; the witness did not stop. Only one testimony was collected. The witness reported his observation three years later. The testimony lacks consistency, as:\n\n- The observation includes many details despite being old and made under poor conditions, while driving at 130 km/h and looking backward;\n- The hypothesis of a reflection off closed windows is not entirely ruled out, although it was mentioned and rejected by the witness.\n\n- The observation took place in a highly emotional context, induced by the feeling of being observed, a feeling present even before the observation, and which seems to have led the witness to remember details or comparisons related to a \"watching eye.\"\n\nTherefore, GEIPAN classifies the case as C: lack of reliable information. Note: The witness had made a similar observation (a tracking eye on the highway) two weeks earlier. Case AIX-EN-PROVENCE (13) 05.10.2004",
          "translation_text_sha256": "ce36ae33c71be3ea0960d71458a64d45361c90cd172c58e9a81d06c3d3092dbf"
        }
